Z||000018||TRiAD||06-11-2001||09:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> Got mine for $9000. '91 Stealth AWD T/T, fully loaded w/ 97K miles but a new engine. Right now with the very few things I've done And for under $13K I can smoke a C5.  <BR> *<BR>BTW, drednot, go **** yourself. Come back when you're not a moron. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hehe, was that entirely necessary?<P>So, in "smoking a C5" you're saying your car does 0-60 in a lot under 4.8sec? A lot would be at least .5sec, so you can do 0-60 in 4.3 or better? Let's see (pulling out current R&T) what kind of company do you keep? <BR>Faster than an NSX, the new M3, ALL the Vettes, (including the Z-06), tied with the Vipers, beat all the Ferraris except the 360 Modena (tie) and the F50, faster then a new Cobra R, Diablo VT Roadster, Esprit V8, ALL the Porsches except the 911s Turbo and GT1, faster than the RUF (Porsche) 3400S and RGT...<I>really</I>. <P>Sorry, but I'm not buying it. I'm not calling you a liar, but your timing appears to be amiss. How did you come up with your accelleration times?<P>BTW, in stock form, ALL the car mags called the 3000GT/Stealth twins (in comparison with the 300ZX TwinTurbo) "a sloppy, overweight, hair-raising ride that could produce quick times, but was clearly more a "sporty" car, than a true sports car."<BR>In having driven both extensively, I must concur. <P>||||reg||5
