Z||000022||FieroMaster88||06-12-2001||12:52 AM||||Ok....specs on the cars.  The 3000GT VR4 came with twin turbo chargers, twin intercoolers, all-wheel drive, four-wheel steering, electronicaly controlled suspension, active aero sistem, active exhaust and more, more...In stock form she will produce 320 horsepower.  Another guy with a 95 said his had 370 HP with a handfull of mods (boost controler, intake, exhaust,HKS Sequential Blow-Off Valve) If thats all it takes to get 70 more HP....what will happen when he upgrades the turbos???<P>The Z06 Vette comes with  a removible hard top and a 5.7L V8 which pumps out 385HP and that is rear wheel drive. <P><BR>"When engaged, the active aero system inclines the spoiler and lowers the air dam whenever the 3000GT rises above 50mph.  It automatically retracts when the speed goes below 30mph."  Bet you wont find that on your vette......<P>All this about the VR4 and i am a GM lover....but this is a great sports car by Mitsubishi.<P><BR>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">         <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles   <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroMaster88 (edited 06-12-2001).]||||reg||4
