Z||000035||danny boy||06-12-2001||05:44 PM||||  I only have one time slip. It was last year when my car was completely stock and my very first time at a dragstrip. I ran a 21.somethin @ 27.98mph. Oh, and I screwed up the launch and missed second gear. I STILL beat the 78 Gremlin I was racing.<BR> I have raced a  chevette on the street and won stoplight to stoplight. I have raced a pinto and won (those things are acually kinda slow). There is a black 4cyl mustang in town, but I haven't had a chance to track him down yet. <BR> <BR> The 3KGT/Stealth is not a sports car. It is a GT car. I can in no way outhandle a C5 and I know this( not from experience.) With everything I've done and running 15 lbs of  boost I am hoping to run it the high/mid 18s.<BR>    Test and tune thursday nights in Greensburg, PA.<BR>  Right now when I bring on boost in second gear I lose traction. I have AWD. Hmmm...<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by danny boy (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000036||Seanh||06-12-2001||06:54 PM||||Anyone know of any timeslips on a Lincoln Mark 8? I can vouge for those things being damn fast with little to no mod's. I (ok, its mommies, too expensive for me) have a '98 Mark VIII and I'v smoked mustangs and Camaros all night with that thing. I love it, but couldn't afford it to save my life.||||reg||1
Z||000037||TRiAD||06-12-2001||07:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B>  I only have one time slip. It was last year when my car was completely stock and my very first time at a dragstrip. I ran a 14.somethin @ 99.98mph. Oh, and I screwed up the launch and missed second gear. I STILL beat the 70 Charger I was racing.<BR> I have raced a vette on the street and won stoplight to stoplight. I have raced a Ferrari 308 and won (those things are acually kinda slow). There is a black Viper GTS in town, but I haven't had a chance to track him down yet. <BR> <BR> The 3KGT/Stealth is not a sports car. It is a GT car. I can in no way outhandle a C5 and I know this( not from experience.) With everything I've done and running 15 lbs of  boost I am hoping to run it the high/mid 12s.<BR>    Test and tune thursday nights in Greensburg, PA.<BR>  Right now when I bring on boost in second gear I lose traction. I have AWD. Hmmm...<P> And where in the hell did you get a C4 was fast? Geesh.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>...I've heard that one before...<BR>The few who are backing you up keep using one word...<I>feel</I>. <BR>My GTI VR6 <I>felt</I> fast, but it was "only" a 6.8 sec car to 60. <P>It's summer, go get another slip, or quit claiming automotive god-hood. <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000038||FieroMaster88||06-12-2001||07:34 PM||||Who the hell said anything about "automotive god-hood"???  He was only saying his stealth was faster than a C5 Vette...which it probably is.  It is amazing what upgrading turbo's and such can do to a car.  The GSX Eclipse with a 2.0L 4 cyl turbo feels fast, and for a car of its size and HP (220) it was pretty damn fast.  He said he can loose traction in second gear...with AWD.  Takes some power to do that.  But what does it matter if it is faster than a C5 vette.  If you dont believe that the Stealth/3000GT's are fast, go drive one (with awd and twin turbo).  WHat are you out to proove anyway?  Do you have a C5 Vette that you have to defend?  How about a Ferrari?  Didnt think so..........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">         <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles   <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroMaster88 (edited 06-12-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000039||danny boy||06-12-2001||09:21 PM|||| I don't have current numbers yet-give me time to get up there. All I said was I can(have) outran a chevette.<BR> If it makes anyone feel any better, My Fiero is a POS. I think it handles great but it has been so long since I drove it I don't remember. It has a worn out Celebrity motor in it and an automatic. there is no paint on it, the interior is all torn up and it smells funny. But if I had to choose between both my Fieros and my Stealth, the Fieros stay. Like Ed Parks told me "9000 could do a lot with a Fiero." Hehe, yep.<BR> Thatrickguy: Buy a Talon/Eclipse. They are easier to work on,more reliable and a WHOLE lot less expensive to buy parts for.My friend has a 91 Eclipse an his car can walk all over me.<BR>------------------<BR>don't push the A/c button.. it catches the car on fire          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg">   <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by danny boy (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000040||87GTBro||06-12-2001||10:37 PM||||My ultimate dream car is a 1996 Mitsubishi 3000GT VR-4.  The ultimate car!!!  If you know anything about the 3000GT... the spyder was only made in 1995 and 1996 and it has an automatic retractable hardtop.  It is awesome!  Push a button and the trunk opens and the top folds back neatly into the trunk.  Trunk closes...... Convertible!!!!!<P>I had the opportunity to see one near Houston one time.  I was drooling!<P>If anyone has one they want to give me... e-mail me...  (I won't trade my Fiero for it though!  I am keeping that!)||||reg||1
Z||000041||TRiAD||06-13-2001||05:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>Who the hell said anything about "automotive god-hood"???  He was only saying his stealth was faster than a C5 Vette...which it probably is.  It is amazing what upgrading turbo's and such can do to a car.  The GSX Eclipse with a 2.0L 4 cyl turbo feels fast, and for a car of its size and HP (220) it was pretty damn fast.  He said he can loose traction in second gear...with AWD.  Takes some power to do that.  But what does it matter if it is faster than a C5 vette.  If you dont believe that the Stealth/3000GT's are fast, go drive one (with awd and twin turbo).  WHat are you out to proove anyway?  Do you have a C5 Vette that you have to defend?  How about a Ferrari?  Didnt think so..........   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1) He said he spend "very little" on the upgrades, and upgrading the Turbos is very pricey. <BR>2) I believe I mentioned I <B>have</B> driven <I>several</I> of them. Yup, they're quick. (sloppy as all get-out, but quick), but that's not the issue. He said he could "smoke C5 'Vettes, and with very little $ spent on mods". <BR>3) I have nothing to prove. I believe <B>he</B> was the one with the big claims about <B>his</B> car, when someone else called it r!ce. <P>L8rs!<P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
