Z||000049||danny boy||06-14-2001||06:16 PM||||R&T August 1995<P> 1994 3000GT VR-4 $43,736 <BR>HP=320 0-60=5.7, 1/4 mile 14.2 Top speed 159mph, 60-0 braking 122', skidpad=.86g, slalom=63.7<BR> The only difference between the 91-93 cars and the 94+ cars is HP 300 Vs. 320(91-93 cars ran 9.5 boost 94+ran 12), newer cars had larger brakes which are a bolt on for the early cars, and 91-93 didn't have a 160mph electronic limit. Oh, the'94+ got the projection headlights.<BR> Heres what I have:<BR>13G turbo upgrade=$1700<BR>450cc injectors(from eclipse) free<BR>Extreme motorsports 3" downpipe $320<BR>3" Catco highflow cat$50<BR>gutted precats=free<BR> 3" cat back exaust $120<BR>Flowmaster3"in/dual2.5"out for Camaro $80<BR>K&N FIPK $129<BR>Extreme motorsports boost controller=$100<BR>Accel plug wires $56<BR>Grand total for go fast parts are $2555 + shipping costs,tax,etc. the rest was interior goodies and other stuff to keep the car healthy and nice. Turbo timer, VDO boost,water,oil guages, new tires 245/45-17 stock size, etc.<P>I run either stock or 15# boost on street and either 87 or 94 octane gas(depends on if I'm out to play or not.)<BR> I raced the chevette with 94 octane running 15# boost. I won. He was pissed, but a little amazed.  <p>[This message has been edited by danny boy (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
