Z||000051||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||08:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B> PICS! We want to see pics! That's gotta be a killer swap.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>How much does a Conquest weigh, anyhow?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>wide-body 3050#<BR>flat body 2800# <P>Should have pics of MY swap up soon...check out other v8 StarQuest on my web page:<BR> <A HREF="http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1/conquest.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.talkcity.com/speedwaydr/vinc1/conquest.html</A> <P>Have a link for a small block chevy Quest and small block ford Quest.<P>Steven<P><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000052||Songman||06-14-2001||08:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>Anyone know of any timeslips on a Lincoln Mark 8?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Before or after the air bag suspension explodes and cost your $2400 to fix? I guess it is a little faster with the front bumper dropped like that.. Now if the back goes first it will probably slow you down...<P>Personally, I don't even know why I opened this thread.. I have no interest in any of this. hehe<P>I sold my Corvette last year and I can tell you that it was nothing to my 911 Targa. Actually, the Corvette was nothing next to my V12 Jag after you gave the 12 time to get up to speed...<P>Anyway.. who cares? My little 4-cylinder Indy ain't fast. But my Lexus is. I don't care if it was made in Japan... <P>Rock on, boys...<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000053||drednot||06-14-2001||09:54 PM||||The air bag suspension lasts a long time, and is reliable.  The reason everybody thinks it costs so much to fix is because no one knows how to work on it but the dealer!!  the compressor costs no more than an A.C. compressor the lines never go bad, the regulator never goes bad, the air bags are not that hard to replace (unless you are stupid).  I just hate it when I see Such a nice car driving around with a collapsed airbag system, and it's so easy to fix!!!   <P>BTW-- Lincoln mark 8 stock 0-60 -- 6.8 - 7 seconds (depending on the source)  <P>That is very good for a stock luxo cruiser that weighs that much.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000054||danny boy||06-14-2001||10:19 PM||||Dreadnot- I'm sorry bout how I introduced myself. I was in a bad mood to begin with, and I hate it when somebody uses the term rice out of text. When I was on the 3KGT forum, everyone talked mad stuff about rice cars. <BR>Turbo cars are very easy to make crazy fast-my first mod was a $2 fishtank valve from WalMart that got me 14#boost.BIG difference.<P>OK here it is: my Stealth is slow. I couldn't outrun a 305 Fbody if it had flat tires. My car is the worst handling car on the road,gets terrible gas milage and girls laugh at me when I drive by. I'm so embarassed by it but I know I can never sell it because I couldn't get half of what I have in it. I should have bought a Honda Civic instead.||||reg||1
Z||000055||FieroMaster88||06-14-2001||11:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B>Turbo cars are very easy to make crazy fast-my first mod was a $2 fishtank valve from WalMart that got me 14#boost.BIG difference.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm....I want a turbo.....<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000056||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||11:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B> Hmmm....I want a turbo.....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I love my turbo cars. 5 min job netted me 15psi of boost from 7.5 stock. Simple twist of a nut on the wastegate actuator. Turbos are fun untill they break!<P>Steven<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||14
Z||000057||Songman||06-15-2001||01:58 AM||||Hmmmm.. I know I posted another response here about my buddy's shop replacing airbags in a Mark VIII this week.. the point that it is not a dealer only fix... and the fact that parts alone were well over $1000 for just the front...<P>Also told about the Lincoln Owner response board where EVERY owner that responded call their cars beautiful, but underpowered, gas hogging, and expensive to maintain mostly because of the air bag suspension that the owners poll said if you get over 60k out of them it is a miracle! EVERY owner complained about air bag suspension. <P>Not trying to prolong this crazy thread or say I know everything. This came straight from a 'Lincoln owner' site. Not me...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
