Z||000059||drednot||06-15-2001||09:04 AM||||Where are these $1000 rubber air bags / sensors coming from??  the dealer??  You can get them for cheep if you know where to look.  BTW -- mine has over 160,000 miles on it (I bought with over 100,000) and my air bag suspension still works fine.  That is not to say it has not had serious work before I bought it, but I thought I would give you a few real life figures.  But, finally we get some truth from Danny boy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000060||Raydar||06-15-2001||09:36 AM||||This may be a stupid question...<BR>Doesn't the Mark VIII use the same basic platform as the T-Bird?<BR>Couldn't you swap in the T-Bird suspension? <BR>Or are all the mounting points different?<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 06-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000061||TRiAD||06-15-2001||10:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B>Dreadnot- I'm sorry bout how I introduced myself. I was in a bad mood to begin with, and I hate it when somebody uses the term rice out of text. When I was on the 3KGT forum, everyone talked mad stuff about rice cars. <BR>Turbo cars are very easy to make crazy fast-my first mod was a $2 fishtank valve from WalMart that got me 14#boost.BIG difference.<P>OK here it is: my Stealth is slow. I couldn't outrun a 305 Fbody if it had flat tires. My car is the worst handling car on the road,gets terrible gas milage and girls laugh at me when I drive by. I'm so embarassed by it but I know I can never sell it because I couldn't get half of what I have in it. I should have bought a Honda Civic instead.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Huh?<BR>From your earlier post, your car is not a '95, so you cannot base the cost of your car on a '95. If you could, I'd recommend the Spyder, as they were closer to $80K, and would make it look even more like you owned an expensive exotic, like you were trying to make it look. Even with upgrades, you still cannot use the '95 times to base your performance on. Your car is not a '95. <P>At any rate, I think this horse was dead long ago. I'm glad you enjoy your car, it is a nice car, just be careful with reckless claims (there's always someone who will prove you wrong...). <P>...Nothing makes a decent car look like crap like a false claim on it's performance.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Have a good one!<P>||||reg||5
Z||000062||BV MotorSports||06-15-2001||11:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by drednot:<BR><B>the thing aboyr 2Xing your boost, it you 1/2 your engine life.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How so? Are you basing that on ........?<BR>I am by no means a mechanical engineer or even a turbo "specialist" but I know the turbos I have dealt with, the turbo'ed cars I have tinkered on and a stack of books that have learned (at least a basic knowledge of) design, installation and theory for turbo systems and I have yet to break or significantly reduce engine life on any turbo car I have "turned up".<P>Now if you take a clapped out 90psi cylinder pressure motor and add more boost, your asking for trouble. <P>Steven<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||5
