Z||000065||FieroMaster88||06-15-2001||04:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by drednot:<BR><B>Where are these $1000 rubber air bags / sensors coming from??  the dealer??  You can get them for cheep if you know where to look.  BTW -- mine has over 160,000 miles on it (I bought with over 100,000) and my air bag suspension still works fine.  That is not to say it has not had serious work before I bought it, but I thought I would give you a few real life figures.  But, finally we get some truth from Danny boy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The only place you can find the air bag suspension for cheap is a salvage yard...for NEW parts it is expensive.  A friend of mine has them on his car....the pump and hoses went bad....so no inflating bags....<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||1
